TI  - Post-intubation tracheal injury: report of three cases and literature review.
PG  - 809-13
LID - S1806-37132009000800014 [pii]
AB  - Post-intubation tracheal injury is a rare and potentially fatal complication. 
      Among the most common causes, cuff overinflation and repetitive attempts of 
      orotracheal intubation in emergency situations are paramount. Diagnosis is based 
      on clinical and radiological suspicion, confirmed by fiberoptic bronchoscopy. 
      Both conservative and surgical management apply, and the decision-making process 
      depends on the patient profile (comorbidities, respiratory stability), 
      characteristics of the lesion (size and location) and the time elapsed between 
      the occurrence of the injury and the diagnosis. We report the cases of three 
      patients presenting tracheal laceration due to traumatic orotracheal intubation, 
      two submitted to surgical treatment and one submitted to conservative treatment.
