TI  - Laryngeal involvement in two severe cases of childhood tuberculosis.
PG  - 1136-8
LID - 10.1097/INF.0b013e3181ac7b26 [doi]
AB  - Laryngeal tuberculosis in children is seldom reported in the literature. We 
      present 2 children from Cape Town, South Africa who had disseminated tuberculosis 
      involving the cervical lymph nodes and the larynx. The cases emphasize the 
      pathophysiology, the clinical picture, the bronchoscopic appearance, and the 
      response to therapy in laryngeal tuberculosis.
