TI  - Primary benign bronchial schwannoma presenting as asthma.
PG  - 856-7
AB  - Recurrent wheezing in children is frequently due to asthma and responds to 
      bronchodilator therapy. We report a case of a 13-year old boy with a 2-year 
      history of presumed asthma not responding to bronchodilator therapy. Bronchoscopy 
      revealed a right main bronchus tumor, which was diagnosed as bronchial schwannoma 
      after resection by sleeve lobectomy. We review the literature on this tumor.
