TI  - Endobronchial schwannoma with massive hemoptysis.
PG  - 89-92
AB  - A 56-year-old man was admitted to our hospital with a complaint of massive 
      hemoptysis. Bronchoscopy revealed a tumor obstructed the orifice of the right 
      lower lobe bronchus. The diagnosis of endobronchial schwannoma was made by 
      broncho-fibroscopic biopsy. Schwannomas are benign tumors which originate from 
      schwann cells. They rarely occur in the trachea or bronchus. On the other hand 
      symptoms in pulmonary schwannoma are usually mild. Massive hemoptysis is 
      extremely rare. We report a case of endobronchial schwannoma complicated by 
      massive hemoptysis.
