TI  - [Pulmonary Langerhans' cell histiocytosis--case report].
PG  - 199-202
AB  - Authors report a case of a 29-year old patient with pulmonary Langerhans' cell 
      histiocytosis who presented with chest pain as a consequence of rib osteolytic 
      process. We carried out a diagnostic work-up which included laboratory and 
      radiographic analysis, lung function tests, bronchoscopy, cytologic and 
      pathologic analysis. After reaching the diagnosis, corticosteroid therapy was 
      introduced with long-term follow-up. In this report, we included a brief review 
      of pulmonary Langerhans' cell histiocytosis.
