TI  - [Dislocation of voice prostheses. Interdisciplinary management of diagnostics and 
      treatment].
PG  - 1126-30
LID - 10.1007/s00106-009-1928-x [doi]
AB  - Tracheoesophageal voice prostheses after total laryngectomy are infrequently the 
      cause of severe complications. We report on a patient with threefold dislocation 
      of a Provox prosthesis, each with suspected oesophageal loss. The patient came to 
      our hospital with acute dyspnoea. An urgent bronchoscopy showed two prostheses in 
      the right and one in the left main bronchus, which had caused inflammation with 
      extensive occlusion of the bronchus. All three prostheses could be recovered.
