DP  - 2009 Jun
TI  - Endotracheal surgery for leiomyoma of the trachea.
PG  - 206-8
AB  - A 61-year-old male was found to have a tracheal tumor, which was noted at the 
      time of screening by a chest X-ray study. The tumor arose from the membranous 
      portion 4 cm above the carina and was proven by biopsy to be a leiomyoma. Because 
      the disease is a benign tumor, all methods for resection, including bronchoscopic 
      techniques, were thus considered. We performed an endotracheal operation via a 
      window made by an incision of the cartilagenous portion, and removed the tumor 
      through an anterior approach. This type of endotracheal operation is one of the 
      surgical procedures for the removal of benign tracheal tumors.
