TI  - Massive cerebral air embolism after bronchoscopy and central line manipulation.
PG  - 67-9
LID - 10.1177/0218492309102501 [doi]
AB  - A 50-year-old woman who underwent double-lung transplantation suffered a massive 
      cerebral air embolism with severe neurological impairment and temporary 
      hemodynamic deterioration after surveillance bronchoscopy and central line 
      removal. We hypothesize that this was due to microscopic pulmonary parenchymal 
      injury during bronchoscopy as well as air entrainment during removal of the 
      central venous line, with subsequent transpulmonary passage into the cerebral 
      vessels.
