TI  - Successful intubation using a simple fiberoptic assisted laryngoscope for 
      Treacher Collins syndrome.
PG  - 1031-3
LID - 10.1111/j.1460-9592.2009.03122.x [doi]
AB  - A fiberoptic-assisted laryngoscope (FLS) (Acoma Medical Industry Co. Ltd., Tokyo, 
      Japan) is a modified Macintosh laryngoscope with a tubular holder into which a 
      fiberoptic bronchoscope can be inserted. We present three cases of Treacher 
      Collins syndrome whose tracheas were successfully intubated with the aid of the 
      FLS. These cases suggest that the FLS may be a useful alternative in the case of 
      difficult pediatric intubation.
