TI  - Centrally located squamous cell carcinoma of the lung mimicking endobronchial 
      tuberculosis.
PG  - 1178-9
LID - 10.1097/JTO.0b013e3181b28f2f [doi]
AB  - Here we report a case of centrally located squamous cell carcinoma of the lung 
      mimicking endobronchial tuberculosis. On the basis of the white light 
      bronchoscopic (WLB) findings, bronchial tuberculosis was initially suspected. But 
      transbronchial biopsy of the lesion revealed squamous cell carcinoma. 
      Autofluorescence imaging bronchovideoscopy (AFI) showed the lesion area as 
      magenta. After four cycles of chemotherapy, the magenta area was markedly shrunk 
      on AFI. Performance of AFI might be useful for differentiating centrally located 
      lung cancer from endobronchial tuberculosis.
