TI  - [A case of paragonimiasis miyazakii suspected after pathologic examination and 
      subsequently confirmed].
PG  - 232-6
AB  - A 58-year-old man presented with right backache and bloody sputum. Chest X-ray 
      revealed a nodular opacity in the right lung. Since could not obtain a diagnosis 
      by bronchoscopy, we performed a lower lobectomy. Histopathologically, there were 
      irregularly shaped necrotizing granulomas and an area of acute hemorrhagic, 
      eosinophilic abscess. We suspected paragonimiasis. The diagnosis of 
      paragonimiasis miyazakii was confirmed by ELISA. This is a valuable case of 
      suspected paragonimiasis confirmed pathologically.
