TI  - Endobronchial band.
PG  - 37-8
LID - 10.1097/LBR.0b013e3181906c49 [doi]
AB  - A 52-year-old man underwent a diagnostic bronchoscopy for right hilar mass and 
      ipsilateral upper lobe endobronchial lesion. During the procedure, a 
      nonobstructing endobronchial tissue band was found on the left main bronchus just 
      before the secondary carina. This tissue formation, of uncertain etiology, did 
      not obstruct the airway or compromise the clearance of secretions and for these 
      reasons it was left intact.
