TI  - Abnormal orientation of Amplatzer PDA device on a chest radiogram masking foreign 
      body aspiration.
PG  - 1559-62
LID - 10.1016/j.ijporl.2008.06.012 [doi]
AB  - Foreign body aspiration and consequent atelectasis of the lower lobe of the left 
      lung with rotation of the heart resulted in an unusual radiographic appearance in 
      a young girl who had recently undergone transcatheter closure of a patent 
      arterial duct and coil embolization of an aortopulmonary collateral. The 
      patient's chest radiography, who was originally admitted at a center with no 
      echocardiography availability, was interpreted as showing embolization of one or 
      both devices. Only clinical evaluation and echocardiography confirmed appropriate 
      device position. Subsequently, foreign body aspiration was suspected and 
      confirmed at bronchoscopy, and successfully treated. Atelectasis resolved within 
      few days.
