DP  - 2008 Feb 1
TI  - Histopathologic consideration of fiducial gold markers inserted for real-time 
      tumor-tracking radiotherapy against lung cancer.
PG  - 382-4
AB  - PURPOSE: Internal fiducial gold markers, safely inserted with bronchoscopy, have 
      been used in real-time tumor-tracking radiotherapy for lung cancer. We 
      investigated the histopathologic findings at several points after the insertion 
      of the gold markers. METHODS AND MATERIALS: Sixteen gold markers were inserted 
      for preoperative marking in 7 patients who subsequently underwent partial 
      resection of tumors by video-assisted thoracoscopic surgery within 7 days. 
      RESULTS: Fibrotic changes and hyperplasia of type 2 pneumocytes around the 
      markers were seen 5 or 7 days after insertion, and fibrin exudation without 
      fibrosis was detected 1 or 2 days after insertion. CONCLUSIONS: Because 
      fibroblastic changes start approximately 5 days after gold marker insertion, 
      real-time tumor-tracking radiotherapy should be started >5 days after gold marker 
      insertion.
