PG  - e246-7
AB  - A male neonate presented at 24 hours with stridor and respiratory distress. 
      Flexible bronchoscopy showed pharyngomalacia, i.e. complete pharyngeal wall 
      collapse during inspiration. Assessment of upper airway dynamics is emphasised. 
      Pharyngomalacia seems to be a self-limiting condition in our case.
