TI  - [Use of endobronchial valve in postresection empyema and residual cavities with 
      bronchopleural fistulas].
PG  - 46-9
AB  - The results of treatment are analyzed in 78 patients with brochopleural fistilas 
      after lung surgery. A method for imaging the draining bronchus under endoscopic 
      guidance, by using the foamed dye administered into the residual cavity, has been 
      developed. A valvular bronchial blocker for abolishing the function of 
      bronchopleural fistular inserted into the lobular and segmental bronchus at 
      bronchoscopy was designed and clinically tested. This procedure allows resurgery 
      to be avoided in 91.7% of cases.
