TI  - Awake intubation using fast-track laryngeal mask airway as an alternative to 
      fiberoptic bronchoscopy: a case report.
PG  - 429-31
AB  - Patients with rheumatoid arthritis (RA) pose a unique challenge to the 
      anesthetist. The manifestations of RA may include cervical spine instability, 
      limited range of motion, and temperomandibular joint involvement limiting mouth 
      opening. Therefore, securing the airway while maintaining the head and neck in a 
      neutral position is of particular concern to the anesthetist. While this is most 
      commonly accomplished using an awake fiberoptic technique, the following case is 
      presented as a safe and efficient initial alternative to the primary use of 
      fiberoptic bronchoscopy in the appropriate patient population.
