TI  - [Blunt tracheal transection].
PG  - 985-9
AB  - Blunt tracheobronchial injuries are rare, but can be life-threatening. A precise 
      preoperative diagnosis and well recognized plan of surgical treatment, which may 
      be unique for each patient are needed to restore the continuity of 
      tracheobronchial tree in a one-stage intervention. We encountered 2 patients with 
      complete tracheal transection of neck and 1 patient with complete tracheal 
      transection in mediastinum and 15 cm tear in the posterior membranous trachea, 
      whose tracheal injury was difficult to repair using direct intubation of distal 
      airway by bronchoscopy. We achieved a good result of repair using a percutaneous 
      cardiopulmonary support system (PCPS).
