TI  - How a bronchoscopy avoided a pediatric pneumonectomy!
PG  - 107-8
LID - 10.1007/BF02907761 [doi]
AB  - Primary Lung pathology without any intraluminal lesion needs extensive lung 
      resections but It is always necessary to rule out any intraluminal pathology 
      before submitting the patient to a Pneumonectomy. The case described illustrates 
      how a last minute, on the table Exploratory Bronchoscopy revealed a Broncholith 
      which avoided an extensive surgery thus reducing the morbidity.
