TI  - Obstructing tracheal pulmonary Langerhans cell histiocytosis.
PG  - 1057-8
AB  - Pulmonary Langerhans cell histiocytosis, also known as eosinophilic granuloma, is 
      an uncommon interstitial lung disease. A solitary nodule, usually parenchymal, 
      may rarely be the only manifestation of the disease. We describe a case of 
      Langerhans cell histiocytosis presenting as an obstructing tracheal lesion in a 
      55-year-old woman. Following complete resection of the lesion via flexible 
      bronchoscopy, full recovery was achieved. This case represents a unique cause for 
      tracheal obstruction, as well as an unreported manifestation of pulmonary 
      Langerhans cell histiocytosis.
