TI  - Severe sand aspiration: a case report with complete recovery.
PG  - 825-8
AB  - A 5-year-old boy, previously healthy, was admitted to Ratchaburi Hospital after 
      being buried in a sand pile. He presented with dyspnea and tachypnea. Chest 
      radiograph showed opaque particles in both main and segmental bronchi (sand 
      bronchogram). The first attempt of bronchoscopy was unsatisfactory as a 
      considerable amount of sand particles had migrated further into the distal 
      bronchi. A second bronchoscopy was performed with 0.9% saline lavage. Most of the 
      sand particles were successfully removed. Intravenous steroids and antibiotics 
      were administered for treatment. The patient was discharged uneventfully by the 
      end of the first week of hospitalization.
