TI  - Acute obstruction of an endotracheal tube: a case report.
PG  - 62-4
AB  - This report describes a case of sudden ventilatory failure, originally diagnosed 
      as bronchospasm, in a child during general anesthesia. A blood clot impaction in 
      the nasotracheal tube was detected using flexible fiberoptic bronchoscopy. The 
      clot was successfully treated as a result of its passage. We hope this report 
      will stress to dental anesthesiologists the intraoperative importance of 
      fiberoptic bronchoscopy not only as an intubation-aiding device but also as a 
      diagnostic and therapeutic tool.
