TI  - Percutaneous tracheostomy: a guide wire complication.
PG  - 891-3
AB  - We report an unusual complication of percutaneous dilatational tracheostomy, in 
      which the guide wire became lodged in the bronchial tree. The assistance of an 
      expert bronchoscopist resulted in successful removal of a fractured J wire with 
      no adverse sequelae for the patient. A subsequent incident has given insight into 
      the mechanism of damage to the guide wire.
