TI  - [Tracheal intubation using a guide wire for a 5-month-old baby with epiglottic 
      cyst].
PG  - 79-81
AB  - We report anesthetic management for a 5-month-old baby with an epiglottic cyst 
      causing stenosis of the upper airway and growth failure. A flexible guide wire 
      was first inserted into the trachea through the forceps port of the fiberoptic 
      bronchoscope (O.D. 3.5 mm) nasally. After removal of the bronchoscope, the 
      trachea was then successfully intubated with a trachea tube (I.D. 3.5 mm) passed 
      over it. Her symptom improved after removal of the cyst. A flexible guide wire 
      combined with fiberoptic bronchoscope is useful in tracheal intubation for a baby 
      with a difficult airway.
