DP  - 2004 Feb
TI  - Glomus tumor of the trachea: value of multidetector computed tomographic virtual 
      bronchoscopy.
PG  - 237-40
AB  - Glomus tumor of the trachea is extremely rare. We report a case of tracheal 
      glomus tumor in a 39-year-old man who presented with hemoptysis. The diagnosis 
      was made after bronchoscopic biopsy of a tumor involving the posterior wall of 
      the upper trachea. Thin-section multidetector computed tomography of the chest 
      was performed before surgical resection, with multiplanar re-formations and 
      3-dimensional virtual bronchoscopic reconstruction. Tracheal sleeve resection 
      with reconstruction was successful, and pathological studies confirmed complete 
      resection and the diagnosis of glomus tumor. The patient was disease-free 3 
      months postoperatively. To our knowledge, this is the first reported case in 
      which additional computed postprocessing was used to help evaluate the extent of 
      such a tumor.
