DP  - 2003 Aug
TI  - Welded tracheal stent removal in a child under cardiopulmonary bypass.
PG  - 294-6
AB  - Metallic tracheal stents have been used in the treatment of paediatric 
      tracheomalacia for more than a decade. We describe a case in which critical 
      airway obstruction occurred during removal of a welded tracheal stent using a 
      rigid bronchoscope under general anaesthesia. Life-saving cardiopulmonary bypass 
      was instituted urgently, and the welded stent was then removed successfully by 
      directly opening the trachea.
