TI  - Treatment of plastic bronchitis in acute chest syndrome of sickle cell disease 
      with intratracheal rhDNase.
PG  - 626-7
AB  - Plastic bronchitis, a condition associated with widespread mucous plugging of the 
      tracheobronchial tree, is an increasingly recognised bronchoscopic finding in 
      acute chest syndrome of sickle cell disease. Removal of casts by bronchoscopy is 
      technically challenging. We describe a child with acute chest syndrome where 
      bronchoscopic removal of extensive tracheobronchial plastic casts was facilitated 
      by intratracheal rhDNase.
