TI  - [A case of aspergillus bronchitis with effective oral itraconazole].
PG  - 282-7
AB  - A 62-year-old woman with diabetes mellitus and chronic hepatitis C was admitted 
      to our hospital because of fever and productive cough. A thoracic CT scan 
      demonstrated a cavity in the left upper lobe, thickening of the bronchial walls 
      and multiple subpleural infiltrates. Fiberoptic bronchoscopy revealed aspergillus 
      bronchitis. The patient was treated with 200 mg/day of oral itraconazole, but no 
      effect was seen. Treatment with 300 mg/day of oral itraconazole, however, 
      resulted in improvement of the symptoms and resolution of the radiographic 
      abnormalities. We report a rare case of aspergillus bronchitis.
