TI  - Sleeve resection of the right main bronchus for postlobectomy broncho-pleural 
      fistula.
PG  - 1020-2
AB  - In this case report we present a novel treatment for bronchial fistula after 
      lobectomy. The patient had right upper lobectomy for T1 N0 M0 peripheral 
      adenocarcinoma and he had been reexplored 4 days later for massive air leak in 
      another chest surgery department. After the reoperation the bronchial fistula 
      persisted and the patient was admitted to our department. Nineteen days after the 
      reoperation, bronchoscopy confirmed that the bronchial stump was totally opened. 
      A sleeve resection to the right main broncus including the fistulous stump of 
      right upper lobe was performed.
