TI  - Pulmonary function tests leading to the diagnosis of vascular ring in an infant.
PG  - 62-6
AB  - A 5-month-old baby was referred to our pulmonary clinic because of chronic cough 
      and wheeze, unresponsive to antiasthmatic treatment. Examination in the Infant 
      Pulmonary Function Laboratory suggested an upper airway obstruction. An aberrant 
      right subclavian artery was subsequently confirmed by a barium swallow, flexible 
      bronchoscopy, and an angiographic reconstructed chest CT study. Due to modest 
      symptoms a conservative medical approach was taken. At follow-up 1 year later, 
      the patient had fewer respiratory and gastrointestinal symptoms.
