TI  - Horseshoe lung with pseudo-ring-sling complex.
PG  - 402-4
AB  - We report on a 1-month-old boy who presented with a "horseshoe" lung, complete 
      "O" rings of the trachea, and an unusual course of the left pulmonary artery 
      mimicking a left pulmonary artery sling. Computed tomography, cardiac 
      catheterization, and bronchoscopy were performed to confirm the rare coexistence 
      of these anomalies. To our knowledge, such a combination of anomalies has not 
      been reported in the English-language literature.
