TI  - Pulmonary sarcoidosis and the acute respiratory distress syndrome (ARDS).
PG  - 655-6
AB  - A 50 year old man presented with 3 weeks of exertional dyspnoea. His chest 
      radiograph on admission revealed diffuse bilateral interstitial infiltrates. He 
      did not respond to antibiotics but subsequently improved on high dose 
      corticosteroids. Bronchoscopic examination with transbronchial biopsy specimens 
      revealed the presence of non-necrotising granulomas. This case demonstrates an 
      unusual clinical presentation of life threatening pulmonary sarcoidosis 
      characterised by the development of acute respiratory distress syndrome (ARDS) 
      with acute respiratory failure.
