TI  - Bronchoscopic needle aspiration biopsy.
PG  - S97-108
AB  - Bronchoscopic needle aspiration biopsy, which encompasses transbronchial needle 
      aspiration, transtracheal needle aspiration, and endobronchial needle aspiration, 
      is a minimally invasive technique used to diagnose mediastinal and pulmonary 
      masses and to stage lung cancer patients with mediastinal lymphadenopathy. Since 
      it is safe, accurate, and potentially cost-efficient, its use may increase in the 
      coming years. It is important that pathologists who examine cytology specimens 
      understand this procedure, its limitations, and ways that it may be optimized.
