TI  - Retrieval of bronchial foreign body with central lumen using a flexible 
      bronchoscope.
PG  - 253-6
AB  - A 5 year-old boy aspirated a metal spring accidentally. The right bronchial 
      foreign body was removed by threading the alligator of a biopsy forceps through 
      the lumen of the spring while opening its jaws distally. This case illustrates 
      that a foreign body with a central lumen in a child can be successfully removed 
      using a flexible bronchoscope, thus obviating the need for general anesthesia and 
      rigid bronchoscopy.
