TI  - [A case of tracheal adenoid cystic carcinoma in a young woman].
PG  - 295-9
AB  - A case of an adenoid cystic carcinoma of trachea is presented. A 30-year-old 
      non-smoking woman with strong inspiratory dyspnea at rest was admitted to the 
      Dept. of Pulmonary Diseases. At auscultation a respiratory murmur was more silent 
      at right lung and stridor over trachea was heard. CT scan revealed tumor at the 
      bifurcation of the trachea. Bronchoscopy was made and biopsy established the 
      diagnosis: adenoid cystic carcinoma. The tumor was partially removed with rigid 
      bronchoscope and radiotherapy was started. Clinical improvement occurred; in 
      control CT scan tumor vanished. The trachea cancers are rare. Symptoms often 
      mimic asthma or chronic bronchitis. Thus in every patient with chronic cough and 
      dyspnea bronchoscopy should be made. A treatment of choice is primary resection 
      and postoperative radiotherapy.
