TI  - Helical CT with multiplanar and three-dimensional reconstruction of nonneoplastic 
      abnormalities of the trachea.
PG  - 400-6
AB  - Helical CT is being increasingly used for the evaluation of suspected tracheal 
      diseases. Although nonneoplastic and noninfectious diseases of the trachea are 
      rare, their appearance on CT images may be highly suggestive of the diagnosis. 
      High quality multiplanar and 3D reconstructions including 3D surface-shaded 
      display and virtual bronchoscopy are helpful to characterize tracheal 
      abnormalities and to demonstrate the location and extent of the diseases.
