TI  - [A case of primary malignant hemangiopericytoma of the lung with marked response 
      to combination chemotherapy with cisplatin, ifosfamide and gemcitabine].
PG  - 373-6
AB  - A 51-year-old man was admitted because of complaints of cough and bloody sputa. A 
      chest CT scan revealed a giant mass lesion in the right middle and lower lobes of 
      the lung and mediastinal lymphadenopathy. Bronchoscopic findings showed a tumor 
      which almost completely obstructed the intermediate bronchus. Histopathological 
      examination of a biopsy specimen demonstrated malignant hemangiopericytoma. Two 
      courses of chemotherapy that combined cisplatin, ifosfamide and gemcitabine were 
      performed every 3 weeks. Both primary lesion and mediastinal lymph node 
      metastases showed marked reduction and toxicity was manageable.
