IS  - 0305-4179 (Linking)
VI  - 27
IP  - 2
DP  - 2001 Mar
TI  - Failure to clear casts and secretions following inhalation injury can be 
      dangerous: report of a case.
PG  - 189-91
AB  - A 27-year-old man suffered smoke inhalation during a fire. Three days later, he 
      complained of respiratory difficulty and was admitted to our hospital. 
      Bronchoscopy revealed a very large buildup of sputum mixed with soot extending 
      from the left main bronchus to the bifurcation of the upper and lower lobe 
      bronchi and causing both pulmonary atelectasis and pneumonia. The debris was 
      successfully removed the next day with basket forceps via bronchoscopy. The 
      patient's airway pressure dropped significantly, enabling extubation almost 
      immediately. Because of the possibility for respiratory failure caused by viscous 
      secretion, it is important to perform initial bronchoscopy in cases of suspected 
      inhalation injury.
