TI  - Diagnosis of tuberculosis.
PG  - 115-8
AB  - Presence of tuberculous infection in the body does not necessarily mean disease. 
      Any diagnostic work up of the disease starts from a high index of clinical 
      suspicion. However, diagnostic modalities include: (a) Isolation of the bacillus; 
      (b) Immunologic tests; (c) Chemical markers; (d) FNAC, bronchoscopy and 
      bronchoalveolar lavage; (e) Amplification systems. There exists controversies and 
      limitations about the disease process even then.
