TI  - Cardiac tamponade secondary to pneumopericardium after lung transplantation: a 
      case report.
PG  - 3123-5
LID - 10.1016/j.transproceed.2008.09.026 [doi]
AB  - Pneumopericardium is a rare cause of cardiac tamponade. It is an exceptional 
      complication of lung transplantation. We have presented a case of a patient with 
      cystic fibrosis who experienced cardiac tamponade secondary to a tension 
      pneumopericardium during the postoperative course after lung transplantation. 
      Dehiscence of the bronchial suture line was confirmed by fiberoptic bronchoscopy.
