TI  - Chamberlain mediastinotomy for diagnosis of adenoid cystic carcinoma of trachea.
PG  - 515-6
AB  - Primary tracheal tumours are extremely rare. Bronchoscopy is the standard 
      diagnostic procedure of obtaining biopsy of a tracheal mass, however it becomes 
      challenging if the obstructing lesion is placed distally along the trachea 
      occluding greater than 90% of the airway. We report the case of a 25-year-old 
      male who suffered from severe tracheal stenosis. The lesion was biopsied through 
      a chamberlain mediastinotomy, under local and mask anaesthesia and was found to 
      be primary adenoid cystic carcinoma.
