DP  - 2007 Apr
TI  - Pulmonary hydatidosis: an unusual cause of haemoptysis.
PG  - 158-60
AB  - A 28-year-old female patient was referred to us with complaints of massive 
      haemoptysis and cough with expectoration, of two years' duration. Her chest 
      radiograph, computed tomography scan and video-bronchoscopy revealed a cystic 
      lesion in the right upper and lower zones of the lungs. Aspiration from the cyst 
      fluid was grossly hemorrhagic and full of inflammatory cells. On digestion of the 
      fluid with potassium hydroxide, it showed plenty of hooklets and scolices of 
      Echinococcus granulosus. An intact brood capsule was also seen. Diagnosis of 
      hydatidosis was further confirmed by a positive serological and therapeutic 
      response to albendazole.
