TI  - A case of bronchial aspiration: the importance of early diagnosis and clinical 
      suspicion.
PG  - 191-3
AB  - We present a case of foreign body aspiration, the diagnosis of which was delayed 
      until two months after the event. This case highlights the importance of a 
      detailed clinical history in establishing the diagnosis of aspiration and how 
      this was complicated by direct visualization via bronchoscopy which suggested a 
      possible diagnosis of bronchial carcinoma. Subsequent histological analysis 
      confirmed a diagnosis of Brazil nut aspiration, which ultimately required 
      surgical extraction through a rigid endoscope.
