DP  - 2006 Nov
TI  - [Tracheobronchopathia osteochondrodysplasias. About one case revealed by 
      haemoptysis].
PG  - 760-2
AB  - Tracheobronchopathia osteochondrodysplasias is a benign and rare chronic disease, 
      whose etiology remains obscure. It is characterized by the presence of 
      subepithelial osteocartilaginous focal lesions without any relation to tracheal 
      rings, essentially localized in the lower two thirds of the trachea and the major 
      bronchi. We report a new case of tracheobronchopathia osteochondrodysplasias in a 
      47-year-old man, localized at the lower half of the trachea, revealed by 
      haemoptysis. The lesion was suspected by bronchoscopy and the diagnosis was made 
      histologically, showing heterotopic bone formation. The evolution of this 
      affection was marked by a good clinical tolerance with only a symptomatic 
      treatment.
