TI  - Bronchoscopic management of airway obstruction in pediatric endobronchial 
      tuberculosis.
PG  - 219-21
AB  - The present report describes a case of severe airway obstruction caused by 
      endobronchial tuberculosis in an 11-year-old girl who was successfully treated by 
      bronchoscopic balloon dilation. This case illustrates the insidious presentation 
      and the increasingly important role of bronchoscopic intervention in the 
      management of endobronchial tuberculosis. In addition, a brief literature review 
      of the condition in the pediatric age group is included.
