TI  - Bronchoscopic diagnosis of an extensive tracheal laceration.
PG  - 534-5
AB  - Tracheal lacerations resulting from endotracheal intubation are extremely rare. 
      We report a case where the initial diagnosis was misled by the radiological 
      findings. Our case uniquely emphasizes several issues pertinent to the management 
      of tracheal lacerations. We review the published works on this topic and 
      emphasize the role of fibre-optic bronchoscopy in the assessment of airway 
      injuries before operative management.
