TI  - Pressure-flow signatures of central-airway mucus plugging.
PG  - 223-6
AB  - SETTING: Medical Intensive Care Unit of Regions Hospital, a University of 
      Minnesota-affiliated teaching hospital. PATIENT: Mechanically ventilated woman 
      with status asthmaticus and acute respiratory failure. INTERVENTION: Observations 
      of airway pressure and flow tracings before and after bronchoscopic inspection 
      and airway lavage. MAIN RESULTS: Four newly observed signs were recorded that may 
      serve to identify occult central airway mucus plugging in the ventilated 
      asthmatic patient.
