TI  - [A case of solitary endobronchial metastasis of hepatocellular carcinoma].
PG  - 422-6
AB  - An 80-year-old man was admitted in October, 2002 with blood-tinged sputum. He had 
      already been treated for hepatocellular carcinoma (HCC). The chest radiograph and 
      chest CT scan showed a solitary pulmonary mass in the left lower lobe. The serum 
      alpha fetoprotein (AFP) was elevated to 261 ng/ml. Fiberoptic bronchoscopy 
      revealed an endobronchial tumor at left B8a and the results of brushing cytology 
      were compatible with HCC. We confirmed the diagnosis by immunohistochemical 
      staining using anti-AFP antibody. Endobronchial metastatis of HCC is rare and 
      immunohistochemical staining was useful for diagnosis.
