TI  - High-frequency jet ventilation through a fibreoptic bronchoscope channel during 
      lung lavage.
PG  - 274-6
AB  - Simple manual ventilation facilitates removal of intra-alveolar accumulations. 
      High-frequency jet ventilation can be performed through a narrow lumen like that 
      of a fibreoptic bronchoscope. Accordingly, we expected that high frequency jet 
      ventilation through a fibreoptic bronchoscope channel would facilitate lung 
      lavage, and we developed a new bronchoalveolar lavage system, in which 
      high-frequency jet ventilation through the channel of a fibreoptic bronchoscope 
      was combined with conventional bronchoalveolar lavage. We describe a case in 
      which this new lavage system, unlike conventional bronchoalveolar lavage, 
      successfully removed the lipid material in the alveoli associated with pulmonary 
      alveolar proteinosis.
