AB  - We report on a patient in whom, 10 months after lung volume reduction surgery, 
      bovine material visibly migrated to the bronchial lumen. In this particular case, 
      bronchoscopic treatment was successful. The patient remained well 12 months after 
      such treatment. The report also suggests that the alternative use of absorbable 
      material will reduce later postoperative complications.
