TI  - Practical issues in autofluorescence bronchoscopy with Storz D Light 
      bronchoscope.
PG  - 247-51
LID - 10.1016/S1572-1000(04)00063-8 [doi]
AB  - Practical aspects of Storz Dlight autofluorescence bronchoscopy are presented 
      from a series of 73 patients. 80 biopsies were taken of which 23 had at least 
      moderate dysplasia, including 8 CIS lesions. Causes of false positive 
      fluorescence abnormalities were suction trauma, overlying mucus, depressions in 
      the leading edge of bronchial spurs, and flexion points of spurs. Positive 
      predictive value of a significant fluorescence abnormality was 56%. The highest 
      yield was in those patients with prior ENT malignancy.
