TI  - [A case of paragonimiasis westermani with a worm migration track on chest CT].
PG  - 463-7
AB  - A 59-year-old man with rusty-colored sputum was admitted for evaluation of a 
      nodular shadow on his chest radiograph. Chest computed tomography (CT) revealed 
      nodules and nodular opacities with a cavity in the right S3. Chest CT also showed 
      clearly a double linear shadow other than the bronchovascular bundle, with a 
      different course from that of the bronchovascular bundle, suggesting a worm 
      migration track. The diagnosis of paragonimiasis westermani was confirmed by 
      detection of Paragonimus eggs in a bronchoscopic aspirate smear and by 
      immunoserological examination. The linear lesion on the chest CT is uncommon in 
      paragonimiasis, but the finding is thought to be useful for the diagnosis of this 
      disease.
