TI  - Mediastinal bronchogenic cyst.
PG  - 64-5
AB  - A 29 year old woman was found to have a chest mass as part of routine screening 
      with a chest x-ray for an unrelated neurosurgical procedure. Further 
      investigation with a chest CT raised the suspicion of a paravertebral neurogenic 
      tumor. The patient underwent bronchoscopy and resection of the lesion by Video 
      Assisted Thoracic Surgery (VATS). The diagnosis of Bronchogenic Cyst was 
      established after histopathologic examination of the resected tumor. Bronchogenic 
      Cysts are relatively rare primary mediastinal tumors. The paravertebral site is 
      an unusual presentation for these tumors.
