TI  - Bronchoscopy in intensive care units.
PG  - S15-9
AB  - Many situations exist imposing the use of bronchoscopy in intensive care units 
      (ICU). There are many diagnostic and therapeutic indications. Interventional 
      bronchoscopy represents a group of endoscopic techniques used in emergency or 
      during the handling of different situations of airway obstruction. These 
      situations seem quite frequent in paediatric ICU. This field has been developed 
      with the availability of small endoscopes on the market and progress in 
      instrumental and anaesthetic techniques.
