TI  - An unusual cause of hemoptysis: ventriculopulmonary fistula.
PG  - 625-7
AB  - A 55-year-old man presented with massive hemoptysis following coronary artery 
      bypass grafting and repair of a left ventricular aneurysm. Radiological and 
      bronchoscopic examinations revealed no bronchial cause. The findings of computed 
      tomography (CT) of the chest and echocardiography showed a pseudoaneurysm of the 
      left ventricle. Surgical exploration confirmed that the pseudoaneurysm 
      communicated with the lung parenchyma.
