TI  - 'Iron lung': distinctive bronchoscopic features of acute iron tablet aspiration.
PG  - 541-3
AB  - Three confirmed cases of acute iron tablet-induced necrosis due to a fulminant 
      chemical burn injury to the tracheobronchial tree as a result of accidental 
      inhalation and/or aspiration of iron tablets are described. Although histological 
      confirmation has been relied upon for diagnosis, the distinctive bronchoscopic 
      features may allow prompt recognition and treatment by bronchoscopists to prevent 
      this potentially fatal condition.
