TI  - Endobronchial tuberculosis complicated with Staphylococcus aureus pneumonia and 
      empyema in a child.
PG  - 254-7
AB  - Childhood tuberculosis might have unusual clinical presentation. A seven-year-old 
      female patient was admitted with fever and pleural effusion. Her pneumonia 
      resolved following 21-day treatment period. An atelectatic appearance remained on 
      the right middle zone in her chest X-ray. Tuberculin skin test showed 13 mm 
      induration. Triple drug antituberculosis treatment was started. Since atelectasis 
      persisted on her follow-up radiograph one month later, bronchoscopy was performed 
      which revealed a hemorrhagic polypoid mass occluding the right upper lobe 
      anterior segment orifice. Surgical removal was performed by right upper 
      lobectomy. The pathological diagnosis was necrotizing granulomatous infection 
      suggesting tuberculosis. The patient has been well on follow-up after completing 
      a nine-month course of antituberculous treatment.
