TI  - Biocides currently used for bronchoscope decontamination are poorly effective 
      against free-living amoebae.
PG  - 784-6
AB  - Free-living amoebae may be pathogenic and harbor several agents of pneumonia. We 
      tested the susceptibility of amoebal cysts and trophozoites to currently used 
      biocides for bronchoscope decontamination. We showed that two particular biocides 
      are inadequate for disinfecting bronchoscopes, as Acanthamoeba polyphaga survived 
      3 hours of exposure to these undiluted agents.
