TI  - Hemoptysis: a rare cause can be related to a bronchial varix due to pulmonary 
      venous obstruction.
PG  - 884-6
AB  - Bronchial varices, which have rarely been described in the radiology literature, 
      can be the result of pulmonary venous obstruction and may present with 
      hemoptysis. This case is an illustration of this rare condition, which correlates 
      CT findings with bronchoscopic findings. We also describe the findings on 
      phase-contrast MR that demonstrated reversed diastolic flow in the branch 
      pulmonary artery supplying the affected lung.
