TI  - A 28 year old woman with ventricular tachycardia and an abnormal chest 
      radiograph.
PG  - e19
AB  - A 28 year old white woman with no medical history presented to the emergency room 
      with symptomatic non-sustained ventricular tachycardia. She was asymptomatic up 
      to a few days before presentation. Her physical examination was essentially 
      normal and hence did not help with the differential diagnosis of the problem. 
      Bronchoscopic transbronchial biopsy led to the final diagnosis of cardiac 
      sarcoidosis.
