TI  - Relapsed non-Hodgkin's lymphoma diagnosed by flexible bronchoscopy.
PG  - 488-90
AB  - Pulmonary relapse of non-Hodgkin's lymphoma (NHL) occurred in a 10-year-old girl 
      who presented with cough, blood-tinged sputum, and chest tightness. The diagnosis 
      of Ki-1 (CD30) anaplastic large-cell lymphoma was established using 
      bronchoalveolar lavage (BAL) and transbronchial biopsy (TBB). These procedures 
      demonstrated malignant cells that stained positive for CD30 and had the t(2;5) 
      translocation, thereby avoiding the need for an open lung biopsy.
