TI  - [Dyspnea, alopecia areata, protrusio bulbi. Which systemic disease is 
      responsible?].
PG  - 42-5
AB  - Sarcoidosis is a systemic disease of unknown etiology and highly variable 
      clinical presentation that manifests most frequently in the hilus lymph nodes, 
      skin and eyes. The present case is a 63-year-old woman who was admitted for 
      investigation of progressive apnea. Numerous typical, but also rare, organic 
      symptoms were assignable to a chronic form of sarcoidosis: epileptiform attacks 
      and depression, as also cutaneous changes affecting the scalp, and long wrongly 
      diagnosed granulomatous "tumour" in the left orbit. The correct diagnosis was 
      established on the basis of bronchoscopy and a chest CT that revealed 
      inflammatory fibrotic changes in the lungs, and the histological work-up of 
      tissue biopsies obtained from the various cutaneous lesions.
