DP  - 2001 Sep
TI  - [Active tracheo-bronchial caseous tuberculosis. Ten patients].
PG  - 289-95
AB  - BACKGROUND: We report 10 cases of active endobronchial tuberculosis in female 
      patients. PATIENTS AND METHODS: Diagnosis of endobronchial tuberculosis was 
      established by demonstrating the presence of Koch bacilli in the bronchial 
      washings or at pathology examination of a bronchial mucosa biopsy. Follow-up was 
      available for 5 of the 10 cases. RESULTS: These women were aged 19 to 756 years. 
      Clinical signs included persistent cough (n=10), wheezing (n=10), dyspnea (n=5), 
      dysphonia (n=4) and fever (n=8). Chest x-ray was normal in 4 cases but showed 
      condensation in 4 others with infiltration of the superior lobe in 2 cases. 
      Bronchoscopy findings were characteristic with a thick layer of white caseum on 
      the mucosa. Koch bacilli were found in all bronchial wash specimens. Pathology 
      examination confirmed the diagnosis of tuberculosis in 5 of the 10 cases.
