TI  - Foreign bodies in the upper aero-digestive tract.
PG  - 117-20
AB  - Foreign bodies in the upper aero-digestive tract pose major challenges to the 
      otolaryngologist in both diagnosis and management. Aspirated and ingested foreign 
      bodies are often emergencies, leading to inadequate study and poorly prepared, 
      improper attempts at removal. The authors share their experience in managing 
      upper aero-digestive tract foreign bodies in Omani population at a district 
      hospital, present a statistical review of 58 cases, and highlight certain 
      critical scenarios as well as cultural variations specific to the region.
