DP  - 2001 Aug
TI  - Herpes simplex virus bronchopneumonia in a non-immunocompromized individual.
PG  - 836-40
AB  - We report a rare case of herpes simplex virus (HSV) bronchopneumonia in an 
      otherwise healthy middle-aged individual. Bronchoscopy indicated scattered 
      white-coated lesions in the bronchial mucosa. The diagnosis was established 
      following immunohistopathological staining for HSV of specimens obtained by 
      bronchial biopsy. This case suggests that HSV could be a pathological agent of 
      not only oral and genital mucosal lesions but also lower respiratory tract 
      infection.
