TI  - Pericardial foreign body.
PG  - 936-8
AB  - The authors describe the case of an inhaled foreign body unusually located in the 
      pericardium. An initial chest skiagram was misinterpreted leading to a negative 
      bronchoscopy. Correct anatomic localization of the foreign body only was 
      established at surgical exploration, despite preoperative computerized tomography 
      scan of the chest. Recognition of the propensity of sharp foreign bodies to 
      migrate is essential in treating these patients. A tracheobronchial foreign body 
      migrating to the pericardium has not been reported previously in the literature. 
      J Pediatr Surg 36:936-938.
