TI  - Management of foreign bodies in the tracheobronchial tree in adults: a 10-year 
      experience.
PG  - 920-3
AB  - OBJECTIVE: To report our experience of foreign bodies in the tracheobronchial 
      tree in adults. DESIGN: Retrospective study. SETTING: Teaching hospital, Athens. 
      SUBJECTS: 25 patients referred to the department of thoracic surgery for 
      treatment. INTERVENTIONS: Bronchoscopic extraction in 16, thoracotomy with 
      bronchotomy in 5, and resection in 4. RESULTS: No major complications and no 
      deaths. CONCLUSION: Bronchoscopic extraction is usually possible, but thoracotomy 
      and bronchotomy or resection may be necessary.
