TI  - A case of endobronchial aspergilloma.
PG  - 422-5
AB  - Pulmonary aspergillosis may be classified under three categories, depending upon 
      whether the host is atopic or immunocompromised: invasive aspergillosis, allergic 
      bronchopulmonary aspergillosis (ABPA) or aspergilloma. However, it is not always 
      possible to effectively categorize this disease. We experienced a case of 
      endobronchial aspergilloma, which was difficult to categorize, in a healthy male 
      patient. The chest X-ray and computed tomography showed an ill-defined nodule 
      mimicking lung cancer. Fiberoptic bronchoscopy revealed an aspergilloma without 
      cavity formation in the left lower laterobasal segmental bronchial orifice. The 
      aspergilloma was removed and the patient's symptoms were relieved. We present 
      this unusual case with a review of the literature.
