TI  - Myoepithelioma of the lung.
PG  - 187-9
AB  - A 54-year-old woman with myoepithelioma, a very rare tumor of the lung, is 
      reported. The patient presented with exertional dyspnea, cough and intermittent 
      pleuritic chest pain. Her chest X-ray revealed a peripheral 2 cm mass in the left 
      lower lung zone. Bronchoscopy was normal. She underwent thoracotomy in which a 
      wedge-resection was performed. Histological examination of the specimen 
      demonstrated myoepithelioma of the lung.
