TI  - Antimicrobial effects of lidocaine in bronchoalveolar lavage fluid.
PG  - 217-9
AB  - The antimicrobial activity of lidocaine in bronchoalveolar lavage fluid (BAL(f)) 
      was investigated. Clinical respiratory isolates were added to BAL(f) suspensions 
      containing lidocaine and to normal saline. The growth of two of four isolates of 
      Streptococcus pneumoniae was significantly reduced in the presence of 
      lidocaine-BAL(f) compared with controls in saline. Growth of Moraxella 
      catarrhalis isolates was reduced in normal saline when compared with BAL(f) 
      containing lidocaine. There was no effect upon the growth of Haemophilus 
      influenzae, Pseudomonas aeruginosa and Candida albicans isolates. The recovery of 
      isolates of S. pneumoniae may be reduced below the critical threshold of 10(5) 
      cfu/mL during bronchoscopy when using lidocaine as a local anaesthetic.
