TI  - A case of tracheobronchopathia osteochondroplastica diagnosed by fiberoptic 
      bronchoscopy upon removal of an aspirated crown.
PG  - 63-7
LID - 10.1155/DTE.7.63 [doi]
AB  - Tracheobronchopathia osteochondroplastica (TO) is a relatively rare benign 
      disease, around 300 and 130 cases have been reported in English and Japanese 
      literature, respectively. Most of the cases have been diagnosed incidentally at 
      autopsy. Due to the widespread use of fiberoptic bronchoscopy (FOB), the number 
      of cases diagnosed upon examination is increasing. Here, we report a case of a 72 
      year-old man with a history of crown aspiration, who was diagnosed as TO upon 
      removal of a foreign body using FOB. The diagnosis of TO and the removal of an 
      aspirated crown by FOB are discussed.
