TI  - Early lung disease in young children with primary ciliary dyskinesia.
PG  - 514-6
LID - 10.1002/ppul.20792 [doi]
AB  - Primary ciliary dyskinesia (PCD) is an autosomal recessive disease in which 
      ciliary dysfunction leads to chronic lung, sinus, and middle ear disease. PCD is 
      often not diagnosed until late childhood due to its presumed rarity and the 
      technical expertise necessary for diagnosis; as such, little is known about lung 
      disease in young children with PCD. We report on 3 young children with PCD who 
      had evidence of lung disease on infant pulmonary function testing, bronchoscopy, 
      and/or computed tomography (CT) of the chest before 3 years of age.
