TI  - Unforeseen scenario in removal of a tracheobronchial foreign body.
PG  - e10-1
AB  - Tracheobronchial foreign body aspirations occur most commonly in children but 
      under certain circumstances, are seen in adults. Majority of patients can 
      successfully be managed via bronchoscopy. However, unexpected complications may 
      develop during the removal procedure. We describe an unusual complication 
      encountered during the removal procedure of an inhaled scarf pin in the trachea 
      of a 23-year old woman. Crucial removal procedure is implicated and awareness of 
      this rare complication is emphasized.
