AB  - We report the case of a 52 years old patient with clinic of food regurgitation 
      and some dysphagia without other added symptoms who was sent to our ENT 
      consulting rooms. It was performed a cervicothoracic CT which informed as a 
      paratracheal cystic lesion with differential diagnosis between esophageal or 
