AB  - We present a case of a patient with severe multiple trauma who was treated at the 
      scene by a physician-staffed trauma life support team. Due to a complete tracheal 
      transection, a "cannot ventilate, cannot intubate"-situation occurred. The 
      patient was then intubated using a fiberoptic bronchoscope in the prehospital 
      setting. The current literature concerning fiberoptic intubation in emergencies 
      is discussed.
