TI  - Inflammatory myofibroblastic tumor of the trachea.
PG  - 847-50
AB  - Inflammatory myofibroblastic tumor of the trachea is a rare benign tumor in 
      children. We describe a 9-year-old girl who presented with recurrent episodes of 
      wheeze and severe respiratory distress requiring mechanical ventilation. She had 
      recurrent collapses of the right lung and a chest CT and bronchoscopy confirmed 
      the presence of an obstructing mass lesion at the carina. The lesion, 1.5 cm x 
      1.5 cm in size, was debulked by rigid bronchoscopy and histopathology revealed 
      features of inflammatory myofibroblastic tumor. A repeat bronchoscopy at 1 month 
      of follow up did not reveal any residual lesion.
