DP  - 2007 Mar 26
TI  - Treatment of bronchial airway obstruction using a rotating tip microdebrider: a 
      case report.
PG  - 16
AB  - BACKGROUND: Central airway obstruction is a common complication of lung cancer. 
      The microdebrider is a new device available for treatment of central airway 
      obstruction. CASE DESCRIPTION: We report a case a 59-yr-old male with T3N2M1 
      non-small cell lung cancer with malignant distal left mainstem obstruction 
      treated successfully with a novel elongated rotating tip microdebrider via rigid 
      bronchoscopy with sufficient length to reach distal bronchial lesions. DISCUSSION 
      AND CONCLUSION: The microdebrider is an excellent addition to the spectrum of 
      interventions available for the management of central airway obstruction with 
      advantages including accuracy and immediate removal of debris without a need for 
      separate suctioning or limitation in oxygenation.
