TI  - [Angioedema caused by C1-esterase inhibitor deficiency or ACE inhibitors?].
PG  - 335-6, 338
AB  - A 49-year-old woman was admitted to the intensive care ward with increasing 
      shortness of breath due to a massive soft tissue swelling of the neck and face 
      and a marked macroglossia. Similar symptoms were already observed earlier in the 
      patient as well as her father, although such symptoms were never as dramatic as 
      they were on this occasion. The patient was intubated bronchoscopically and 
      treated unsuccessfully with cortisone, fresh plasma und C1-esterase inhibitor. 
      The patient only first reported intake of an ACE inhibitor a few days after the 
      acute episode, which was most probably the causative factor given that serum C1 
      and C4 complement factors were almost normal.
