TI  - [Torsion of the right upper lobe due to primary lung cancer with pulmonary 
      hypertrophic osteoarthropathy; report of a case].
PG  - 1213-6
AB  - A 61-year-old woman was admitted due to severe coughing. Chest X-ray revealed a 
      mass in the right lower lung field at standing position and in the right upper 
      lung field at supine position. A position of the mass changed with change in her 
      posture because of lobar torsion. Bronchoscopic biopsy of the polypoid tumor 
      obstructing the right upper bronchus revealed adenocarcinoma. She had 
      hypertrophic osteoarthropathy simultaneously. Right pneumonectomy was performed. 
      Postoperative course has been uneventful for 3 years.
