DP  - 2005 Sep
TI  - Lung volume reduction surgery.
PG  - 363-75
AB  - Lung volume reduction surgery (LVRS) has been widely studied and has been 
      available for the treatment of advanced emphysema for 10 years. This paper 
      reviews some of the historical attempts at surgical treatment of emphysema, the 
      physiology of LVRS, and the modern data on patient selection, risks, and 
      benefits. Data from the National Emphysema Treatment Trial are presented in the 
      context of the large body of case series and smaller randomized trials that have 
      preceded that study. Future technologies of bronchoscopic lung volume reduction 
      are also discussed.
