TI  - Solitary metastasis of lung carcinoma to the internal auditory canal.
PG  - 214-6
AB  - We report a case of solitary metastasis of lung carcinoma into the internal 
      auditory canal. On admission, the 60-year-old patient was complaining about a 
      rapidly developing hearing loss with ipsilateral facial nerve paralysis. Magnetic 
      resonance imaging revealed an intracanalicular tumor, which was interpreted as 
      vestibular schwannoma. After tumor resection, the histopathologic examination 
      revealed a metastasis of a squamous cell carcinoma. Computed tomographic scan and 
      bronchoscopy identified an asymptomatic primary pulmonary neoplasm.
