TI  - [Fatal pulmonary mucormycosis in a diabetic patient].
PG  - 40-2
AB  - We report a case of pulmonary mucormycosis in a 65-year-old diabetic patient. 
      Pulmonary mucormycosis should be suspected in predisposed patients presenting a 
      pneumonia that resists to antibiotics. The microbiologic diagnosis requires 
      usually a biopsy using bronchoscopic or surgical procedures. The optimal therapy 
      requires an early systemic antifungal treatment associated with the resection of 
      the pulmonary lesion and the control of the underlying disease.
