DP  - 2004 Dec
TI  - Carcinoma in situ from the view of complete resection.
PG  - 383-5
AB  - World Health Organisation (WHO) defined three types of preinvasive epithelial 
      lesions, one of which is preinvasive bronchial squamous lesions consisting of 
      dysplasia and carcinoma in situ (CIS). It is not clear whether or not CIS at the 
      bronchial resection margin is to be considered as incomplete resection in the 
      literature. Follow-up data of such patients using autofluorescence bronchoscopy 
      proved that CIS regresses without further treatment in significant number of 
      patients. It is therefore reasonable to accept any reported CIS lesion on 
      frozen-section examination as complete clearance of the tumor and thus further 
      resection may not be warranted.
