TI  - Adenoid cystic carcinoma of trachea.
PG  - 287-9
AB  - A 20-year-old male, presented with cough, haemoptysis, breathlessness and 
      wheezing for the past one month. Contrast enhanced computerised tomographic 
      (CECT), scan of chest and fibreoptic bronchoscopy revealed an endotracheal mass 
      that on histopathological examination showed adenoid cystic carcinoma of trachea. 
      Magnetic resonance imaging (MRI) scan of chest confirmed involvement of adjacent 
      prevertebral, para-oesophageal and subcarinal lymph nodes rendering the tumour 
      inoperable.
