TI  - Catamenial pneumothorax and other thoracic manifestations of endometriosis.
PG  - 311-9
AB  - Thoracic endometriosis syndrome is an uncommon entity with varied clinical 
      manifestations. Its pathogenesis is not understood completely. Recurrent 
      unilateral right-sided pneumothorax that occurs within days of the onset of 
      menstruation is the most common presentation. Clinical suspicion and recognition 
      of the temporal relationship of the patient's symptoms with menses are essential 
      to establish the diagnosis. Radiographic studies, bronchoscopy, and thoracoscopy 
      may support the diagnosis. Pathologic evidence of thoracic endometrial tissue is 
      not present universally. Therapeutic interventions, which include medical and 
      surgical options, must be individualized for each patient.
