TI  - [A case of an uncommon foreign body in the esophagus].
PG  - 747-50
AB  - Esophagial foreign bodies are mostly located in the sites of the physiological 
      and pathological narrowings. A case of 58 year old patient with profound mental 
      impairment, who swallowed a stone of 3 cm in diameter and a molar tooth has been 
      presented. The treatment and prognosis was complicated by retention of barium 
      contrast in the lungs. The patient underwent the bronchoscopy and double 
      esophagoscopy. Foreign body was successfully removed through external approach 
      (oesophagotomy).
