TI  - Prevention and management of complications of airway surgery in children.
PG  - 107-11
AB  - Preventing and managing complications of airway surgery in children requires 
      proactive attention to both surgical and anaesthetic aspects of the planned 
      procedure. Preoperative evaluation should include a thorough physical examination 
      and, especially in children with multiple congenital anomalies, flexible 
      fibreoptic nasopharyngolaryngoscopy, direct laryngoscopy and rigid or flexible 
      bronchoscopy. The goal is to identify dynamic abnormalities such as 
      laryngomalacia or vocal cord paralysis, tracheal or bronchial lesions, 
      gastro-oesophageal reflux disease (GORD), aspiration, laryngotracheal stenosis, 
      totally obstructing tracheostomy-associated granulation tissue and Noonan 
      syndrome preoperatively, and then to plan surgical management to achieve the best 
      possible outcome for each patient.
