TI  - Purulent pericarditis induced by endobronchial needle injection of 
      adenoviral-mediated gene therapy.
PG  - 1421-3
AB  - A case of a 65-year-old man who presented with cardiac tamponade and was 
      diagnosed with Staphylococcus aureus purulent pericarditis is reported. The 
      patient had recently undergone bronchoscopic endobronchial needle injection of 
      gene therapy for recurrent lung cancer. It was felt that incidental, direct 
      inoculation of contaminated contents into the pericardium, versus mediastinal 
      seeding with direct extension, had occurred. Following pericardiocentesis and 
      antibiotic therapy, the patient fully recovered. The present case is the first 
      reported incidence of purulent pericarditis induced by bronchoscopic injection of 
      gene therapy.
