TI  - [A case of large-cell lung cancer with liver metastasis successfully treated 
      using combination chemotherapy with CDDP and vinorelbine].
PG  - 1787-90
AB  - A 38-year-old woman presented to our hospital with the chief complaint of 
      dyspnea. A chest radiograph showed pleural effusion of the right lung and a CT 
      scan revealed liver metastasis. A tumor biopsy done under bronchoscopy revealed 
      large-cell carcinoma of the lungs. She was given 4 courses of a combination 
      therapy consisting of CDDP (80 mg/m2) and vinorelbine (25 mg/m2). The primary 
      tumor in the right lung and liver metastasis were markedly reduced in size and a 
      partial response was obtained. The combination therapy of CDDP and vinorelbine 
      may become a standard chemotherapy for advanced non-small cell lung cancer.
