DP  - 2002
TI  - Lung abscess (6 cm) of unexplained origin in a 36-year-old woman.
PG  - 481-2
AB  - A 36-year-old woman developed a lung abscess following an episode of influenza. 
      Repeated blood cultures were negative. In necrotic material obtained by 
      bronchoscopy no pathogenic micro-organisms were found. Penicillin-clavulanate, 
      cefodizim and metronidazole were without success. The combination therapy with 
      imipenem-cilastatin together with clindamycin improved clinical symptoms, 
      normalized pathological laboratory parameters and completely resolved the lung 
      cavity.
