TI  - Successful one-lung ventilation in a patient with aberrant tracheal bronchus.
PG  - 492-3, table of contents
AB  - We report a 47-yr-old patient who underwent surgery for esophageal cancer. 
      Because of the isolated ventilation of the right upper lobe after occlusion of 
      the right mainstem bronchus, bronchoscopic re-confirmation exposed an aberrant 
      tracheal bronchus. A Fogarty tube was introduced to block the tracheal bronchus 
      and provide one-lung ventilation.
