TI  - H-type tracheoesophageal fistula: report of one case.
PG  - 100-1
AB  - An H-type tracheoesophageal fistula (T-E fistula) is a rare congenital 
      abnormality. The diagnosis is made using an esophagogram and/or endoscopy. Early 
      diagnosis of this disorder is still a challenge to pediatricians. Surgical repair 
      is the standard treatment for patients with H-type tracheoesophageal fistulae. 
      Recently, some bronchoscopic procedures have been developed to obliterate the 
      fistulae.
