TI  - Airway obstruction due to bilateral giant pulmonary artery aneurysms.
PG  - 366-8
AB  - Large pulmonary artery aneurysms are rare, but they are associated with 
      significant morbidity and mortality. Significant airway obstruction due to 
      extrinsic compression solely by a pulmonary artery aneurym is an extremely rare 
      occurrence. We present a case of large bilateral pulmonary artery aneurysms 
      causing extrinsic airway compression with collapse of the left primary bronchus 
      in a 51-year-old woman. This is the first report in an adult in which airway 
      compression due solely to the pulmonary artery aneurysm resulted in airway 
      collapse. Furthermore, we describe the use of interventional bronchoscopy with 
      stent placement as a minimally invasive alternative to surgery for treatment of 
      these patients.
