TI  - Bronchoscopy and needle biopsy techniques for diagnosis and staging of lung 
      cancer.
PG  - 137-58, ix
AB  - Lung cancer is the leading cause of cancer deaths in the United States. The 
      individual therapeutic approach and prognosis depends on accurate diagnosis and 
      staging. Flexible bronchoscopy (FB) and transthoracic needle biopsy (TNB) are the 
      most widely used techniques for this purpose. This article provides a critical 
      overview of indications, diagnostic yield, and limitations of bronchoscopy and 
      TNB in the diagnosis of lung cancer.
