TI  - [Serotonin level in endocrine cells in bronchial mucosa and stomach in chronic 
      obstructive lung diseases].
PG  - 26-9, 96
AB  - 85 patients aged 26-60 years with pulmonary chronic obstructive diseases (PCOD) 
      and gastric and duodenal erosive-ulcerous lesions were investigated. In PCOD the 
      increased bioamines level in endocrine cells of bronchial ciliated epithelium and 
      gastric glandular epithelium was detected before the treatment. The complex 
      treatment in the form of bronchoscopy with lymphotropic administration of 
      antibiotic and immunomodulator against the background of intragastral 
      ozonotherapy contributes to the decrease in tissue edema, restoration of their 
      trophicity and inflammatory process resolution. Against the background of therapy 
      the serotonin content in endocrine cells of bronchial ciliated epithelium and 
      gastric mucosa decreased to the norm.
