TI  - [Diagnosis and treatment of primary pulmonary rare malignant tumors].
PG  - 466-8
LID - 10.3779/j.issn.1009-3419.2001.06.20 [doi]
AB  - BACKGROUND: To explore the clinical features, diagnosis and treatment of primary 
      pulmonary rare malignant tumors. METHODS: Forty-nine patients with primary 
      pulmonary rare malignant tumors were retrospectively analysed about their 
      clinicopathological characteristics and X-ray signs, as well as methods of 
      diagnosis and treatment. RESULTS: Among 49 patients, which was 0. 70% ( 41/ 5 
      872) of all pulmonary tumors resected in the same period, 1 case was diagnosed by 
      bronchoscope biopsy, 2 cases by lymph node biopsy, and 4 cases by pulmonary 
      puncture and biopsy. Another 41 cases ( 83. 6%, 41/ 49) underwent surgical 
      operation and were pathologically diagnosed after operation. CONCLUSIONS: 
      Surgical operation is main measure in the diagnosis and treatment of primary 
      pulmonary rare malignant tumors.
