TI  - Granular cell tumor of the bronchus.
PG  - 425-8
AB  - Persistent atelectasis and recurrent pneumonia in the same location should raise 
      suspicion of congenital anomalies or obstructing lesions of the bronchus leading 
      to the affected area. We present an 8-year-old black female with a history of 
      recurrent fever, cough, atelectasis of the right middle and lower lobes, and 
      weight loss for several months. Flexible bronchoscopy revealed a polypoid mass 
      obstructing the bronchus intermedius. Biopsy of the neoplasm demonstrated a 
      granular cell tumor (GCT). The patient had a lobectomy of the right lower and 
      middle lobes. She had no recurrence of the tumor after several years of 
      follow-up.
