DP  - 2000 Jul
TI  - Organization of personnel and resources for airway management in the hospital and 
      office environment.
PG  - 527-39, viii
AB  - Good airway management depends on a system that emphasizes teamwork to expedite 
      care and minimize errors. By understanding the accreditation and licensing 
      requirements, appropriate personnel and equipment can be allocated along cost 
      effective guidelines. Newer techniques for management of the difficult airway, 
      such as the laryngeal mask airway (LMA; LMA North America, San Diego, CA) and 
      flexible fiberoptic bronchoscope, provide alternatives to the emergency 
      cricothyrotomy. A program of continuous quality improvement and clinical 
      guidelines will enhance patient care and suggest intelligent use of airway 
      resources.
