TI  - Congenital tracheobiliary fistula.
PG  - 149-52
AB  - Congenital respiratory tract-biliary fistula, including tracheo- and 
      broncho-biliary fistulae, are rare developmental anomalies. To date, only 18 
      cases have been reported. We present two additional cases that came to our 
      attention after a long and difficult attempt to make a diagnosis. After surgical 
      excision of the tract both children have remained symptom-free for 6 and 4 years, 
      respectively. Bronchoscopy allows an early diagnosis, but patients also have to 
      be investigated for associated biliary tree malformations.
