DP  - 2000 May
TI  - [Blunt tracheobronchial injuries in children].
PG  - 206-10
AB  - Blunt tracheobronchial injuries in children are rare and are associated with many 
      diagnostic problems. Based on the successful outcome in a seven- and a 
      twelve-year-old patient operated within 12 hours after the accident the authors 
      discuss the development of the symptomatology and early clinical, X-ray, 
      bronchoscopic and CT diagnosis of rupture which are, if intensive care and early 
      treatment of the injury are ensured, the basis for preserving normal pulmonary 
      function and ensure prevention of sequelae due to obstruction and infection. The 
      children were admitted to hospital for 22 and 14 days resp. and discharged in a 
      good condition. The check-up examinations of both patients are within the normal 
      range and there are no limitations as compared with healthy children of the same 
      age.
