TI  - Laser resection of a pedunculated tracheal adenoma.
PG  - 262-6
AB  - We report a case of tracheal adenoma presenting as hemoptysis and reversible 
      airflow obstruction in an ex-smoker. A questionable defect in the tracheal air 
      shadow on a posteroanterior chest radiograph was shown on CT to be a 
      pedunculated, mid-tracheal tumor. Two-stage bronchoscopic laser resection 
      resulted in an apparently normal tracheal mucosa. Results of postresection 
      spirometry were normal.
