TI  - Recurrent lower respiratory tract infections in a 14-year-old boy with 
      tracheobronchomegaly (Mounier-Kuhn syndrome).
PG  - 476-9
AB  - Tracheobronchomegaly (Mounier-Kuhn syndrome) is characterized by dilatation of 
      the central airways, tracheobronchial outpouchings, and chronic 
      tracheobronchitis. Most cases are diagnosed in adulthood. We report the clinical, 
      radiographic, and bronchoscopic findings in a 14-year-old boy with 
      tracheobronchomegaly, ptosis of the right eyelid, and redundant skin and mucosa 
      of the upper lip, who presented with a 2-year history of recurrent lower 
      respiratory tract infections. Pediatricians should be aware of the possibility 
      that tracheobronchomegaly may cause clinical symptoms in childhood and 
      adolescence. Pediatr Pulmonol. 2000; 29: 476-479.
