TI  - Fibreoptic intubation under general anaesthesia--a simple method using an 
      endotracheal tube as a conduit.
PG  - 296-300
AB  - A novel technique for management of the difficult airway is described. The case 
      report describes fibreoptic intubation of a patient who refused awake intubation. 
      An endotracheal tube was advanced as far as the nasopharynx via the nostril of 
      the patient, under anaesthesia. Connection of the anaesthetic circuit allowed 
      maintenance of anaesthesia, oxygenation and assisted ventilation while flexible 
      bronchoscopy was performed through the tube via a bronchoscopy connector The 
      endotracheal tube was subsequently advanced over the bronchoscope into the 
      trachea. This technique uses readily available materials and can be used where 
      the placement of a laryngeal mask is contraindicated or impossible.
