TI  - Intrabronchial foreign body extracted with tranilast and corticosteroid.
PG  - 1686-8
LID - 10.1016/j.athoracsur.2008.04.060 [doi]
AB  - We present a case of intrabronchial foreign body buried in granulation tissue, 
      which was successfully extracted administrating tranilast 
      (n-[3,4-dimethoxycinnamoyl] anthranilic acid), suppressing collagen synthesis by 
      fibroblasts in keloid and hypertrophic scars, and corticosteroid. Bronchoscopy of 
      a 74-year-old man showed the nail was buried in reactive granulation tissue and 
      could not be observed from the surface. Tranilast at 300 mg/day and 
      methylprednisolone at 250 mg/day were prescribed for 4 days, followed by a 
      reduction of the corticosteroid to 40 mg/day for 3 days. Seven days later, the 
      granulation tissue and mucosal edema were diminished, and the nail was 
      successfully extracted.
