DP  - 2008 Oct 31
TI  - Extranodal marginal zone lymphoma occurring along the trachea and central airway.
PG  - 860-3
LID - 10.3349/ymj.2008.49.5.860 [doi]
AB  - Extranodal marginal zone lymphoma is a low-grade B cell lymphoma that presents 
      with an indolent clinicopathologic nature. Although this tumor can occur in 
      various sites, including the gastrointestinal tract and lungs, it develops and 
      spreads extremely rarely along the trachea and central airway. We report a case 
      of extranodal lymphoma of mucosa-associated lymphoid tissue with tracheobronchial 
      involvement. An 83-year-old woman presented with a cough and dyspnea. 
      Bronchoscopic evaluation confirmed diffuse, multiple nodular lesions in both the 
      trachea and large bronchi, and she was diagnosed with an extranodal marginal zone 
      lymphoma of the tracheobronchial tree. After systemic chemotherapy, she survived 
      for more than 18 months.
