DP  - 2008 Jun
TI  - [Intrathoracic ectopic kidney in an adult: case report and bibliographic review].
PG  - 631-3
AB  - OBJECTIVE: We report the case of a 61-year-old male with the incidental diagnosis 
      of intrathoracic renal ectopia during the workup study for a possible lung mass. 
      METHODS: We performed a bibliographic review on the incidence, origin, clinical 
      presentation and diagnosis of this type of renal ectopia. RESULTS: Chest x-ray 
      showed a left posterior mediastinum mass. Bronchoscopy was performed showing 
      signs of extrinsic compression with absence of neoplastic cells. CT scan revealed 
      a left intrathoracic ectopic kidney with diaphragmatic hernia. CONCLUSIONS: 
      Intrathoracic renal ectopia is a very unfrequent finding, often asymptomatic, 
      frequently an incidental diagnosis that does not require treatment.
