TI  - [Respiratory morbidity after pulmonary resection; prevention and treatment of 
      atelectasis and pneumonia].
PG  - 710-4
AB  - A respiratory morbidity such as atelectasis or pneumonia is possible to be 
      predicted by calculated postoperative pulmonary function. The predicted 
      postoperative 1 second forced expiratory volume (FEV1.0) is exclusively useful 
      for predicting morbidity, but not for predicting mortality. The exercise capacity 
      is a crucial parameter to predict survival. Thus, both parameters are helpful to 
      make strategies for perioperative management. A prophylactic tracheostomy, a 
      timely traheostomy and a timely bronchoscopy are applied by these parameters to 
      treat postopeartive respiratory complications such as atelectasis or pneumonia.
