TI  - Reimplantation of the left lung 17 years after a bronchial rupture.
PG  - 1436-8
LID - 10.1016/j.athoracsur.2007.09.002 [doi]
AB  - We describe a 37-year-old female patient who had a major vehicle accident 17 
      years ago. A chest tube had been inserted through the left side of the chest to 
      treat pneumothorax. She was readmitted to the hospital with dyspnea 17 years 
      later. Her examinations, including fiberoptic bronchoscopy, revealed total 
      atelectasis of the left lung with a blind-ending left main bronchus. Anastomosis 
      of the left distal main bronchus to left main bronchus was performed. She had no 
      complications and was discharged on postoperative day 8. Follow-up demonstrated a 
      perfectly functioning left lung with nuclear and tomographic investigations 
      performed on the first postoperative year.
