AB  - Complete rupture of the main bronchus after blunt thoracic trauma is rare. Most 
      patients with blunt traumatic injury to the trachea or bronchus die before 
      arriving at hospital. A 26-year-old man with complete right main bronchus rupture 
      was successfully treated by urgent surgical intervention and postoperative 
      fiberoptic bronchoscopy for bronchial toilet.
