TI  - [Lung adenocarcinoma feigning an interstitial lung disease in a 30-year-old man].
PG  - 289-91
AB  - A case of a 30-year-old man is presented. He had a past medical history of asthma 
      and presented with cough, shortness of breath, fever and chest pain. The chest 
      X-ray showed cardiomegaly and a interstitial pattern. The echocardiogram revealed 
      a severe pericardial effusion that required performing a pericardiocentesis. A CT 
      scan showed mediastinal adenopathies and reticulonodular interstitial pattern. A 
      bronchoscopy could not be completed because of non-tolerance. Finally a lung 
      biopsy allowed us to reach a final diagnosis of lung adenocarcinoma. Following, 
      some aspects of lung cancer in young people are commented, especially its 
      incidence, histology, symptoms and a prognosis. A few aspects of the interstitial 
      lung disease are also addressed and the differential diagnosis with lymphangitic 
      carcinomatosis.
