TI  - Migration of surgical sponge retained at mediastinoscopy into the trachea.
PG  - 637-40
AB  - It is uncommon to find an iatrogenic foreign body after thoracic surgery. We 
      present a case of migration of a surgical sponge left inadvertently in the 
      mediastinum during a troublesome mediastinoscopy, that migrated into the trachea 
      6 years later with airway obstruction. The foreign body was extracted through 
      rigid bronchoscopy and the patient had a full recovery.
