TI  - Giant tracheocele following primary tracheostomy closure in a 3 year old child.
PG  - 411-2
AB  - Tracheocele is a rare pathology, especially complication of tracheal surgery. We 
      present a case of a 3 year old pediatric patient with secondary tracheocele 
      arising after simple surgical closure of tracheostomy. It appeared 2 months after 
      intervention that cervical mass swelling during respiratory acts. Diagnosis was 
      made by TC scan and by dynamic flexible bronchoscope which revealed a substomal 
      segmental tracheomalacia. Surgical procedure consisted of simple excision of 
      tracheocele associated with enhancing tracheomalacic segment by free graft of 
      costal cartilage as Cotton procedure. Follow up at 14 months demonstrated a 
      patent of cervical trachea without any sign of malacia.
