TI  - Whistle in the bronchus.
PG  - 124-5
LID - 10.4103/1817-1737.33702 [doi]
AB  - An 18-year-old male presented with 4 weeks' history of productive cough and fever 
      that had started 1 day after alleged ingestion of a plastic whistle. Multiple 
      courses of antibiotics had proved ineffective. Crepitation and a localized wheeze 
      on right chest were observed on clinical examination. Chest radiograph showed a 
      right-sided pneumonitis. Bronchoscopy revealed a grayish-black foreign body in 
      the right bronchial tree, which was retrieved and found to be the 'lost whistle.' 
      The patient improved dramatically following the procedure.
