TI  - [Lung metastases in a primitive neuroectodermal tumor].
PG  - 35-7
AB  - Primitive neuroectodermal tumor (PNET) is a soft tissue sarcoma and is common 
      among children and young adults. We present a case of a 27 years old woman with 
      PNET localized at left arm and with lung metastases. Local ultrasound of the arm 
      presented a tumor mass of 55/20 mm, computed tomography showed multiple pulmonary 
      nodules in bilateral fields. The biopsy made during bronchoscopy and the biopsy 
      made at arms level described PNET. CD99 markers was positive in both 
      examinations.
