TI  - [Surgical case of bronchopleural fistula caused by necrotizing pneumonia in a two 
      year old child].
PG  - 518-22
AB  - The treatment possibilities of broncho-pleural fistula (BPF) caused by 
      necrotizing pneumonia (NP) are discussed based on the experiences of a case and 
      on the basis of the literature. In case of pleural fluid caused by NP the 
      importance of thoracic drainage and--in selected cases--video assisted 
      thoracoscopy (VATS) are emphasized. If BPF develops and the oxygen saturation in 
      the blood can not be kept on acceptable level because of the large volume of the 
      lost air through the fistula bronchoscopic occlusion of the bronchus leading to 
      the BPF is recommended. In conservative therapy resistant cases thoracotomy can 
      be indicated.
