DP  - 2007 Apr
TI  - Allergic bronchopulmonary aspergillosis coupled with broncholithiasis in a 
      non-asthmatic patient.
PG  - 365-8
AB  - Allergic bronchopulmonary aspergillosis (ABPA), an asthmatic disease, is caused 
      primarily by hypersensitivity to Aspergillus species. ABPA is rarely observed in 
      the absence of asthma, which is, in fact, the principle criterion for its 
      diagnosis. Here, we report the case of a 36-yr-old woman without a history of 
      bronchial asthma, who manifested a localized pneumonic consolidation, coupled 
      with broncholithiasis. Pathologic examinations of bronchoscopic biopsy specimens 
      and resected surgical specimens revealed features typical of ABPA. This is a very 
      rare case of ABPA coupled with broncholithiasis in a non-asthmatic individual.
