TI  - Segmental tracheal dysplasia in a mixed breed dog.
PG  - 1003-6
AB  - A 6-month-old, spayed female, mixed breed dog was referred for respiratory 
      difficulty. Radiographic and bronchoscopic evaluations showed tracheal narrowing 
      from the thoracic inlet to its bifurcation. Under anesthesia, the trachea 
      ruptured and the dog died. Microscopic evaluation revealed underlying segmental 
      tracheal and bronchial cartilaginous malformation (dysplasia).
