TI  - Blunt tracheal transection and long tear in posterior membranous trachea.
PG  - 945-7
AB  - Blunt tracheobronchial injuries are rare, but can be life-threatening. A precise 
      preoperative diagnosis and a well-recognised plan of surgical treatment, which 
      may be unique for each patient, are needed to restore the continuity of 
      tracheobronchial tree in a one-stage intervention. We encountered a patient with 
      complete tracheal transection and 15 cm tear in the posterior membranous trachea 
      and right bronchus, and whose tracheal injury was difficult to repair using 
      direct intubation of distal airway by bronchoscopy. We achieved a good result of 
      one-stage repair using a percutaneous cardiopulmonary support (PCPS).
