TI  - Repositioning a displaced tracheostomy tube with an Aintree intubation catheter 
      mounted on a fibre-optic bronchoscope.
PG  - 576-9
AB  - Although tracheostomy tube displacement is uncommon, the management is often 
      difficult and the associated mortality is high. It is important to ensure that 
      the airway is secure and then either replace or reposition the tracheostomy tube. 
      This case report describes the use of an Aintree intubation catheter 
      (C-CAE-19.0-56-AIC, William Cook Europe, Denmark) mounted on an intubating 
      fibre-optic bronchoscope (11302BD1, Karl Storz Endoskope, Germany) to reposition 
      a partially displaced tracheostomy tube.
