TI  - [Application of flexible bronchoscopy in postoperative management of lung 
      transplantation].
PG  - 1543-5
AB  - OBJECTIVE: To investigate the application of flexible bronchoscopy in the 
      postoperative management of lung transplantation. METHODS: Four male patients 
      with end-stage chronic obstructive pulmonary disease received examination with 
      bronchoscope following the unilateral lung transplant for management of airway 
      complications. One patient developed stenosis at tracheal anastomosis 2 months 
      after transplantation and underwent balloon dilatation and endobronchial metallic 
      stent placement. RESULTS: The 4 patients showed good recovery after 
      transplantation with obviously improved pulmonary function and quality of life. 
      CONCLUSION: Flexible bronchoscopy provides a valuable means for postoperative 
      management of lung transplantation.
