TI  - Successful bronchoscopic retrieval of Timothy grass from the airway.
PG  - E39-41
AB  - Aspiration of Timothy grass in the airway is a well-recognized cause of 
      bronchiectasis, and management often requires pulmonary resection. The authors 
      describe 2 cases of Timothy grass aspiration with established pulmonary infection 
      that were successfully managed by bronchoscopic removal with subsequent 
      improvement. Every effort should be made to accomplish this goal, and pulmonary 
      resection should be considered a last resort in these cases.
