TI  - Spectrally programmable light engine for in vitro or in vivo molecular imaging 
      and spectroscopy.
PG  - 2033-40
AB  - A spectrally and temporally programmable light engine can create any spectral 
      profile for hyperspectral, fluorescence, or principal-component imaging or with 
      medical photonics devices employing spectroscopy, microscopy, and endoscopy. 
      Multispectral imaging feasibility was demonstrated by capturing nine images at 
      wavelengths from 450 to 650 mm (25-nm FWHM) with a CCD-camera-equipped 
      bronchoscope coupled to the light engine. Selected wavelength regions were 
      combined to produce a color endoscopy image.
