TI  - Sedation and fiberoptic intubation of a neonate with a cystic hygroma.
PG  - 122-3
AB  - The flexible bronchoscope (FB) has been used to secure the difficult airway in 
      pediatric patients. Difficult intubations in patients with cystic hygromas have 
      been performed in awake patients or after the induction of general anesthesia. A 
      recent case report acknowledges the challenges of performing intubations in 
      pediatric patients under sedation because of their inability to fully cooperate. 
      The following case demonstrates the two step-two fiberoptic bronchoscopic 
      tracheal intubation performed using sedation and topical anesthesia in a neonate 
      with a difficult airway.
