TI  - [A case of bronchial ulcer due to infection by Mycobacterium abscessus].
PG  - 919-23
AB  - We present a rare case of tracheobronchitis caused by Mycobacterium abscessus. 
      The patient was a 79-year-old man with a previous history of tuberculosis. For 
      smear examinations, he repeatedly expectorated many acid-fast bacilli. 
      Bronchoscopic examination revealed the presence of ulceration on the lower end of 
      the trachea and extending to the right main bronchus. Mycobacterial cultures were 
      used to grow Mycobacterium abscessus. Following an antimicrobial regimen of 
      clarithromycin, amikacin, and cefoxitin, the patient exhibited marked 
      improvement. After initial multidrug therapy, the patient was placed on 
      clarithromycin for 10 months. No relapse has occurred to date.
