TI  - [Fever, coughing and/or wheezing in young children: consider the possibility of 
      foreign body aspiration].
PG  - 1661-5
AB  - Three children, 2 girls aged 1.5 and 3 years and a 2-year-old boy, experienced 
      coughing, wheezing and/or fever for several days or weeks. The first girl was 
      treated for asthma, the other two children for pneumonia. Because the symptoms 
      persisted in all three children after treatment was started, the diagnosis of 
      foreign body aspiration was suggested and confirmed by bronchoscopy. The foreign 
      body was removed during the bronchoscopy and in the boy, a mucosal lesion in the 
      piriform fossa was sutured. Thereafter, all the children recovered completely. In 
      children with persistent coughing, wheezing or fever despite treatment for 
      pneumonia or asthma and in absence of a characteristic acute incident, foreign 
      body aspiration should be considered.
