TI  - Sleeve resection of a transcarinal bronchial carcinoid after laser debulking.
PG  - 1093-5
AB  - We report a case of a bronchial carcinoid tumor extending from the right upper 
      lobe into the left mainstem bronchus in a 30-year-old woman. Diagnosis was 
      established by preoperative bronchoscopy and biopsy. After extensive debulking 
      with seven sessions of bronchoscopic neodymium:yttrium-aluminum-garnet laser 
      therapy, the tumor was resected by right upper-lobe sleeve lobectomy. Final 
      pathology revealed a typical carcinoid tumor with surgical margins and all lymph 
      nodes free of tumor.
