DP  - 2004 Oct
TI  - Acute respiratory distress due to fibrosarcoma of the carina in a child.
PG  - 355-7
AB  - We report a 12-year-old boy with primary bronchopulmonary fibrosarcoma (PBPF). He 
      was misdiagnosed a having asthma until he presented with acute respiratory 
      distress syndrome. Chest x-ray showed atelectasis of the right lung. Bronchoscopy 
      performed to rule out foreign body inhalation revealed a friable mass obstructing 
      the right main bronchus. Successful treatment was achieved with surgical 
      resection of the lesion followed by radiotherapy and chemotherapy.
