TI  - Anesthesia in Beckwith-Wiedemann syndrome.
PG  - 778-80
AB  - Anesthetic management of a 3-month-old boy with Beckwith-Wiedemann syndrome for 
      bronchoscopy is reported. Management may be complicated by a difficult airway, 
      congenital heart disease, and hypoglycemia. We did not have difficulty in airway 
      management either with tracheal intubation or rigid bronchoscopy, but we could 
      not extubate the baby because of tracheomalacia.
