IS  - 0003-4975 (Linking)
VI  - 77
IP  - 5
DP  - 2004 May
TI  - A case of primary diffuse tracheobronchial amyloidosis.
PG  - 1832-4
AB  - Tracheobronchial amyloidosis (TBA) is an uncommon localized form of amyloidosis 
      with fewer than 150 reported cases in the literature. We report a case of primary 
      diffuse tracheobronchial amyloidosis who presented with cough, wheezing, 
      recurrent and progressive dyspnea as well as hemoptysis. Though there is no 
      universally accepted treatment for the localized form, this patient was 
      successfully treated with three sessions of bronchoscopic resection and adjuvant 
      steroids. This report will review the various types of amyloidosis of the 
      respiratory tract and their clinical features, in addition to discussing the 
      different available treatment modalities for TBA.
