TI  - Neonatal necrotizing tracheobronchitis: three case reports.
PG  - 259-60
AB  - Necrotizing tracheobronchitis is a serious affection observed in ventilated 
      newborns, frequently infants with instable hemodynamic state. It is characterized 
      by acute episodes of airway obstruction. The treatment consists of the 
      desobstruction by rigid bronchoscopy. The vascular theory seems to be of utmost 
      importance in the physiopathology. Three cases are reported.
