TI  - The role of bronchoalveolar lavage in the immunocompromised host.
PG  - 87-94
AB  - Bronchoscopy with bronchoalveolar lavage (BAL) is a frequently performed, 
      minimally invasive endoscopic examination in patients with unclear infiltrates or 
      pulmonary infections. It can be performed safely in patients with compromised 
      immune systems of different etiologies. This article summarizes the experience 
      with and efficacy of BAL in different disease states in this clinical 
      circumstance. Because human immunodeficiency virus (HIV)-related diseases and 
      acquired immune deficiency syndrome (AIDS) patients show different 
      characteristics when compared with patients with other reasons for 
      immunosuppression, they are discussed separately. Clinical algorithms are 
      presented.
