TI  - Bronchoscopy and infection.
PG  - 143-6
AB  - Bronchoscopy can be useful to diagnose respiratory infections in the 
      immunocompromised and those with problematic cystic fibrosis or with focally 
      abnormal chest X-rays. Its role in paediatric tuberculosis is controversial with 
      scanty objective evidence. As it is an invasive procedure, the following should 
      be asked: what question am I trying to answer by bronchoscopy? Will the answer 
      justify the risks of the procedure?
