TI  - Acoustic reflectometry detection of an endobronchial intubation in a patient with 
      equal breath sounds.
PG  - 41-7
AB  - Acoustic reflectometry can be used to distinguish between a tracheal and an 
      esophageal intubation based on an area-distance profile. In a patient undergoing 
      laparoscopic surgery, acoustic reflectometry was used to detect a 
      bronchoscopically confirmed endobronchial intubation in the presence of equal 
      bilateral breath sounds. An in vitro simulation suggests that in an endobronchial 
      intubation, in the presence of a space leak between the tube cuff and the 
      bronchus, an acoustic pressure disturbance can be transmitted to the opposite 
      lung (causing equal breath sounds), without significant bulk airway flow (causing 
      inadequate ventilation of the opposite lung).
