TI  - Hypoglossal nerve palsy as complication of oral intubation, bronchoscopy and use 
      of the laryngeal mask airway.
PG  - 239-43
AB  - Hypoglossal nerve injury is a recognized but rare complication of oropharyngeal 
      manipulation during intubation, bronchoscopy and use of a laryngeal mask airway. 
      We present 2 new cases of temporary hypoglossal nerve palsy after orotracheal 
      intubation for general anesthesia. The relevant literature is reviewed and 
      different hypotheses concerning the pathophysiological mechanisms of nerve damage 
      are discussed.
