TI  - [Pseudo-tumoral aspergilloma].
PG  - 431-3
AB  - Aspergilloma is the most common form of pulmonary aspergillosis, generally 
      developing pre-existing lung cavities. Fiberoptic bronchoscopy is required in 
      case of hemoptysis. We report the case of a 74-year-old man with pulmonary 
      aspergilloma where fiberoptic bronchoscopy visualized mycetoma and cavitation. 
      Visualization and biopsy of the fungus ball during fiberoptic bronchoscopy is 
      rare.
