TI  - A case of cough, lymphocytic bronchoalveolitis and coeliac disease with 
      improvement following a gluten free diet.
PG  - 91-2
AB  - Chronic cough is a common reason for presentation to a respiratory clinic. In up 
      to 20% of cases the cause remains unclear after investigations. We report one 
      such case where there was bronchoscopic evidence of lymphocytic airway 
      inflammation in association with newly diagnosed coeliac disease. All features 
      improved markedly on a gluten free diet, suggesting a causal relationship between 
      coeliac disease, cough, and lymphocytic bronchoalveolitis.
