DP  - 2001 Jul-Sep
TI  - Fiberoptic flexible bronchoscopy via the laryngeal mask airway in children.
PG  - 197-9
AB  - The laryngeal mask airway (LMA) is a new device for controlling the airway during 
      many procedures. Aside from its use in different kinds of surgical procedures, 
      fiberoptic flexible bronchoscopy can also be performed easily with this mask in 
      children under sedation. This procedure was performed via LMA in 36 children 
      (aged 2-16 years) who suffered from different kinds of respiratory diseases and 
      were seen at Hacettepe University Ihsan Doğramaci Children's Hospital, Pediatric 
      Chest Disease Unit, during a seven-month period. The procedure was performed with 
      success and no complications occurred. To the best of our knowledge, this is the 
      first report from Turkey on flexible bronchoscopic evaluation via LMA in children 
      with different kinds of respiratory diseases. We suggest that this technique can 
      be used safely.
