DP  - 2001 Oct
TI  - Endobronchial foreign body extraction: a new interventional approach.
PG  - 1402-5
AB  - Endobronchial foreign bodies are often difficult to diagnose as the cause of 
      obstructive pneumonias and atelectasis, but once discovered, they can generally 
      be removed, leading to immediate and dramatic resolution of symptoms. The use of 
      flexible fiberoptic and rigid bronchoscopy to extract foreign bodies is 
      well-known. Thoracotomy is generally reserved as a last resort due to the 
      inherent risks of the procedure. We describe a new technique for foreign body 
      removal utilizing steerable hydrophilic guidewires, standard sheaths, and a snare 
      device commonly utilized in intravascular foreign body retrieval.
