TI  - Fetoscopic temporary tracheal occlusion by means of detachable balloon for 
      congenital diaphragmatic hernia.
PG  - 730-3
AB  - Occlusion of the fetal trachea blocks the egress of fetal lung fluid and 
      stimulates the growth of hypoplastic lungs in fetuses with diaphragmatic hernia. 
      Accomplishing temporary and reversible occlusion of the fetal trachea has proven 
      difficult without invasive fetal surgery. Using simultaneous real-time 
      ultrasonography and fetal bronchoscopy through a single uterine port, we placed a 
      detachable balloon in the trachea of 2 fetuses with severe diaphragmatic hernia. 
      In both fetuses the fetal lung subsequently enlarged, allowing survival after 
      birth.
