AB  - Great advances had been made in rigid instrumentation, with the introduction of 
      the glass rod telescope. With relatively few exceptions, however, bronchoscopy 
      was still performed primarily for therapeutic indications, such as the removal of 
      foreign bodies from the airway. It would remain for the introduction of the 
      flexible bronchoscope to stimulate the widespread development of diagnostic 
      bronchoscopy in pediatric practice.
