DP  - 2001 Jun
TI  - Flexible bronchoscopy in nosocomial pneumonia.
PG  - 263-79, viii
AB  - In this article, an overview on the diagnostic performances of bronchoscopic 
      techniques for the diagnosis of nosocomial pneumonia is given with special 
      emphasis on the inherent problems of the methodology of validation applied to 
      different studies. The current evidence about the importance of bronchoscopic 
      techniques for the outcome is reviewed. It is outlined that future prospects of 
      bronchoscopic investigations mainly include the evaluation of its role in the 
      reassessment of the patient with pneumonia not responding to the initial 
      antimicrobial treatment.
