TI  - Foreign body retrieval in children with respiratory symptoms and no history of 
      aspiration.
PG  - 673-80
AB  - To asses the role of bronchoscopy and its yield in children with respiratory 
      symptoms and no typical history of radiological evidence of foreign body 
      aspiration (FBA), we reviewed the records of all patients who underwent 
      bronchoscopy at our institution between 1985 and 1995 and had no history of 
      choking, witnessed FBA or clear radiological evidence of FBA (N = 54, age range 4 
      months to 16 years). These were subdivided into two subgroups, those with 
      positive bronchoscopy, and those with negative bronchoscopy. Respiratory symptoms 
      and their duration, signs and radiological findings did not differ in both 
      subgroups.
