TI  - [A resected case of multiple lung cancers].
PG  - 345-8
AB  - A 78-year-old man was admitted to our hospital because of abnormal shadows on 
      chest film. A 20 x 25 mm tumor shadow was found in the right lower lung field 
      (S10) and a 5 x 10 mm tumor shadow in the right upper lung field (S2). 
      Bronchoscopic curettage revealed squamous cell carcinoma from the specimen on the 
      S10 and did not revealed malignant cells from the specimen on the S2. He was 
      performed operation, squamous cell carcinoma in the S10 was removed by right 
      lower lobectomy and nodule in the S2 was also removed by partial resection. 
      Histological examination confirmed well-differentiated squamous cell carcinoma 
      from the S10 and well-differentiated adenocarcinoma from the S2. He is healthy 
      three year after operation.
